Task 4 – Payment Processing System
Concepts Used
•	Interface 
•	Abstract class 
•	Inheritance 
•	Method overriding 
•	Runtime polymorphism 
•	Extensibility 
Java Program
import java.util.*;

interface Payment {
    void pay(double amount);
}

class CreditCardPayment implements Payment {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Payment through Credit Card");
    }
}

class UPIPayment implements Payment {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Payment through UPI");
    }
}

class NetBankingPayment implements Payment {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Payment through Net Banking");
    }
}

abstract class PaymentProcessor {

    abstract double processPayment(Payment payment, double amount);
}

class OnlinePaymentProcessor extends PaymentProcessor {

    @Override
    double processPayment(Payment payment, double amount) {

        if (payment instanceof CreditCardPayment) {

            return amount + (amount * 0.02);
        }

        else if (payment instanceof UPIPayment) {

            return amount + (amount * 0.01);
        }

        else if (payment instanceof NetBankingPayment) {

            return amount + (amount * 0.015);
        }

        return amount;
    }
}

public class PaymentProcessingSystem {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int N = sc.nextInt();

        PaymentProcessor processor =
                new OnlinePaymentProcessor();

        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {

            int paymentType = sc.nextInt();
            double amount = sc.nextDouble();

            Payment payment;

            if (paymentType == 1) {
                payment = new CreditCardPayment();
            }
            else if (paymentType == 2) {
                payment = new UPIPayment();
            }
            else {
                payment = new NetBankingPayment();
            }

            double finalAmount =
                    processor.processPayment(payment, amount);

            String paymentName;

            if (paymentType == 1) {
                paymentName = "CreditCard";
            }
            else if (paymentType == 2) {
                paymentName = "UPI";
            }
            else {
                paymentName = "NetBanking";
            }

            System.out.printf(
                "%s %.2f%n",
                paymentName,
                finalAmount
            );
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
Sample Input
3
1 1000
2 2000
3 5000
Calculation
Credit Card:
1000 + (1000 × 2%)
= 1000 + 20
= 1020
UPI:
2000 + (2000 × 1%)
= 2000 + 20
= 2020
Net Banking:
5000 + (5000 × 1.5%)
= 5000 + 75
= 5075
Output
CreditCard 1020.00
UPI 2020.00
NetBanking 5075.00
________________________________________
Important Design Flow
The second program follows this structure:
                Payment (Interface)
                       |
          -----------------------------
          |             |             |
    CreditCard       UPI        NetBanking
          |             |             |
          -------- PaymentProcessor --------
                         |
                OnlinePaymentProcessor
Why is this design extensible?
If we want to add:
WalletPayment
we can create:
class WalletPayment implements Payment {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Payment through Wallet");
    }
}
